dotnet_diagnostic.CA2201.severity = warning # this rule made me realize that invalidoperationexception (and its derived type objectdisposedexception (and probably other derived types)) are *also* precondition checks, but they are precondition checks on the state of the called object, rather than checks on the state of the provided arguments; the name might be slightly misleading (compare to notsupportedexception and overflowexception; those exceptions are the result of "invalid operation"s, but they cannot be checked as precondition requirements (well, maybe notsupported can be, but that's used in design failure situations; the type system should be check those things, not the caller or implementer); i kind of want an analyzer that requires a justification for using `invalidoperationexception`; i also want an analyzer that ensures that argument exceptions are used on arguments specifically (and maybe also before any other logic is run)
# NOTE: there are no rules from CA2202-CA2206
